 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Rites are ceremonies that mark important moments in life and in the community. Common traditional rites in Cameroon:\n• birth: naming ceremonies, presenting the baby;\n• initiation: entry of young people into adulthood or into societies;\n• marriage: introductions, bride price (dowry), the wedding;\n• death: funerals and death celebrations (cry-die), often months or years later;\n• enthronement of a chief or fon; harvest and planting festivals; purification rites.\nEnquiry: choose one rite in your region; ask elders and participants what is done, who takes part, what objects, songs or dances are used, and what it means. Respect secrets that may not be shared, ask permission before taking photos, and write a short report.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "r": "a death celebration (cry-die)"
  },
  "problem": "Plan an enquiry on {r} in your area.",
  "steps": [
   "Questions: When is it held? Who takes part? What is done (songs, dances, food, rituals)? What does it mean?",
   "Sources: elders, the family, a traditional ruler; note names and dates.",
   "Respect: ask permission, respect what may not be shared, write a short report."
  ],
  "answer": "Clear questions, respectful interviews with elders, a short report.",
  "checks": []
 },
